  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.  Extent to which authorities in Bosnia and Herzegovina manage to respond to the emergency needs related to COVID-19 disease outbreak in a timely and coordinated manner.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Target: Highly effective procurement and delivery of medical equipment and supplies</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2021, through the immediate Covid- 19 response intervention, the UNDP delivered total of 3,931,150 pcs of PPE, 306, 108 pcs of tests for detection of COVID-19; 6 stationary X -Ray machines; 41 mobile Ultrasound devices; 3 ventilators for critical care, more than 900 oxygen bottles of different capacities with the flow meters and humidifiers, 5 High Flow Nasal Canula (HFNC) devices, 9 pcs of laboratory equipment etc. These interventions significantly increased capacities of local health actors to effectively deal with Covid-19 pandemic even in the cases of extremely high incidence.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Target: Highly effective.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project established partnerships with and provided support to 96 institutional beneficiaries throughout the country, including clinics, hospitals, health care centers, public health institutes, etc. The project has procured and delivered 9,131,137 pieces of various medical goods, health protection and medical waste management supplies ( 33,241 units of clinical management assets and facilities, including more than 2,300 medical devices and equipment; 8,418,865 pieces of personal protective equipment and disinfectants; 455,736 testing material9 and
100 items of laboratory equipment; 132,385 items medicines; 90,760 items for COVID-related medical waste management; and 49 other medical supplies). These interventions significantly increased capacities of local health actors to effectively deal with Covid-19 pandemic even in the cases of extremely high incidence.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Target: Highly effective procurement and delivery of medical equipment and supplies</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">[12/5 7:48 PM] Dzenan Kapetanovic

In 2022, through the immediate Covid- 19 response intervention, the UNDP delivered total of 191,943 pcs of various medical items and equipment consisting of 191, 924 pcs of tests for detection of COVID-19; 1 laboratory device; 1 Autoclave; 2 stationary X -Ray machines; 7 mobile Ultrasound devices; 1 X-ray diagnostic unit and 27 defibrillators</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
